{
  "case_version": 1,
  "name": "fanout-independent-receipts",
  "description": "A fan-out request injects one independent thread per egress link of its entry proxy. Each branch has its own receipt slot, so a slow branch can never overwrite or mix with a fast one; require_all_branches asks for every branch and the two delays stay within TTL. The pause/resume pair in the timeline is a no-op on the entry proxy: it is placed before anything is in flight, which shows that an empty pause costs nothing and changes nothing.",
